  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": "Please note, there are many applications relating to the Royal Mews - those listed below only relate to the buildings affected in this application. \n00/04524/1884 - Conversion of two self contained flats (35 and 36) into one unit with six bedrooms and shared facilities.\n06/02600/1884 - Alterations including refurbishment of self contained flats within the Back Mews. Installation of raised walkway at first and part second floor levels and creation of new access from Lower Grosvenor Place all as part of enhanced security strategy.\n09/07703/FULL - Repair/refurbishment works to roof of residential accommodation at the Royal Mews, including new aluminium steps, new lantern light, fall safe cable system and new access hatch.\n09/07571/LBC - Repair/refurbishment works to roof of residential accommodation at the Royal Mews, including new aluminium steps, new lantern light, fall safe cable system and new access hatch.\n14/07358/LBC – Fire proofing works to Royal Mews comprising fixing windows shut, replacement doors and installation of fire resistant secondary glazing.\n14/02833/FULL - Installation of roof access hatch, stair and railing above 52 The Royal Mews.\n14/02834/LBC - Installation of roof access hatch, stair and railing with associated internal alterations above 52 The Royal Mews.\n16/08175/FULL - External alterations to roofs including extension of access stair, removal of five existing roof lanterns and disused gantry, rebuilding chimney and new lead covering to part of adjacent canopy.\n16/08176/LBC - External alterations to roofs including extension of access stair, removal of five existing roof lanterns and disused gantry, rebuilding chimney and new lead covering to part of adjacent canopy.\n16/02366/LBC - Refurbishment of roof and brickwork on the Royal Mews 'Bridge Building' to match existing.\n19/01335/FULL - Installation of 2no. EV charging point bollards to The Back Mews, including associated services installation and groundworks.\n19/01336/LBC - Installation of 2no. EV charging point bollards to The Back Mews, including associated services installation and groundworks. (Linked to 19/01335/FULL)",
